; References — the @ marker
;
; CORE spec areas: "References (@)" (selector tuples, inert at core) and
; the @ guard of "Marker Recognition". Interim wire: one Reference event
; carrying the raw text after @.


; Reference (CORE "References", `@`-inert): called with the `@` consumed and
; the current char passing the guard (`[`, `.`, or identifier start). The
; payload is the RAW TEXT after `@` — `@[mit]` -> "[mit]",
; `@license[mit].realized` -> "license[mit].realized" — one uniform rule, no
; information loss (interim wire; structured encoding is a SPEC-CORE open
; item). Trait tails (`.trait`) continue the reference both before and after
; the `[key]` (0.9: selector tuples incl. trait-only `@.realized`). The old
; `:[id]` attribute-merge form is REMOVED (merge is a host resolution mode).
|function[block_ref:Reference]  | MARK
  |state[:main]
    |c['[']                   | ->[']'] | ->                     |>> :post_key
    |c[<XLBL_CONT '.'>]       | ->                               |>>
    |default                  | TERM                             |return

  ; After `[key]`: trait selectors may follow (`@el[key].trait.more`)
  |state[:post_key]
    |c[<XLBL_CONT '.'>]       | ->                               |>>
    |default                  | TERM                             |return
